{
  "$comment": "DDD bridge for the U.S. Web Design System (USWDS) 3 default theme. Tiers follow elements/d-d-d/design-system/bridge/contract.json. The palette comes from USWDS's Sass color maps (scss-map), so named DDD colors map onto USWDS system colors by the roles the default theme assigns (primary blue-60v, base gray-cool, success green-cool, warning gold, the visited-link violet as HAX's incorrect purple). Vivid grades are written as <family>-vivid-<grade> (USWDS writes blue-60v). USWDS has no dark mode, so the theme chrome pairs palette steps with light-dark(). Values USWDS only computes in Sass (fonts, weights, radii, shadows, focus, card and button spacing) are literal entries with a note naming the setting. Kept as DDD on purpose: medium and black weights (USWDS sets none), radius-lg/xl (USWDS stops at 8px plus pill), motion and state opacities (no tokens), control heights, border widths, and heading/body sizes. USWDS's 8px unit sits on DDD's 4px grid. This is an independent HAX integration; it does not include the official U.S. government banner, seals or any identifier that marks a real .gov site.",
